2. Tune the batch auto-routing defaults from ledger evidence
   (`batch_threshold_usd=1.0`, chars/4 token estimate, 1k tokens/image — now
   in `base_llm_service.py`, shared by OpenAI/Claude/Google): once consumers
   accumulate batch usage, compare the estimator against actual per-job cost
   in the psyche cost ledger (usage-hook data) and adjust the default
   threshold/estimator constants. Companion tuning task required by the
   heuristic-number law. [when: real batch usage accumulated in the ledger]
   [by: system] [~1h] [added: 2026-07-30]
   - **Structural sub-item, NOT gated on ledger data (found 2026-08-02 from
     model_internals_safety):** `_estimate_cost_usd` uses `max_tokens` as the
     per-request output estimate. That is a sound proxy for non-reasoning
     models — the guardrail sibling tunes it per model (Llama-Guard 128,
     HarmBench-cls 32) and gets accurate routing — but it is structurally
     invalid for REASONING models, where the API forces a generous completion
     budget to hold hidden reasoning tokens. gpt-5-mini judges at the standard
     `max_tokens: 16384` estimate ~$3.30/job against a real cost near $0.08:
     a ~40x bias no `batch_threshold_usd` value can absorb, so tuning the
     constants cannot fix it. Consequence: every gpt-5-mini judge job in the
     family silently auto-routes to the native batch API. Harmless where no
     GPU is held (it is 50% cheaper), but model_internals_safety calls judges
     synchronously with a model resident on a GPU, where unbounded batch
     latency is charged to the job's wall-clock allocation — it pins
     `use_batch_api: false` locally as the fix at its own layer.
     **Blast radius makes this propose-first, not a drive-by fix:** making the
     estimate accurate would drop most judge jobs below the $1 threshold and
     flip llm_guardrail_security's headline ASR judge from batch to realtime,
     roughly DOUBLING its judge API bill with no visible change. Preferred
     shape: an explicit `expected_output_tokens` hint on the service seam,
     defaulting to `max_tokens` so no existing consumer's routing moves;
     reasoning-model callers pass a real figure. Needs a tag + consumer
     pin-bumps, so it rides a deliberate release, never an experiment
     deadline. [by: system] [~2h] [added: 2026-08-02]
